(Software Test Plan \(STP\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(Purpose: verify the SRS functional, non-functional and security requirements through unit, API,) Tj
T*
(system, browser and acceptance testing. Scope: passenger registration, authentication, search,) Tj
T*
(booking, simulated payment, cancellation, admin management and recovery. Exclusions: real payment) Tj
T*
(settlement, real refund transfers, provider email/SMS delivery and production availability) Tj
T*
(certification. Reference: Documents/Software_Requirements_Specification.md,) Tj
T*
(Documents/Software_Architecture_and_Design.md.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Test items) Tj
T*
(React frontend, Django API and services, MySQL schema and transactional behavior, session/CSRF) Tj
T*
(protection, admin controls, CI pipeline and recovery procedures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Features to be tested) Tj
T*
(SRS F-001 020; NF-001 005; SR-001 005. High-priority scenarios: authorization, search and inventory,) Tj
T*
(atomic booking and PNR creation, payment confirmation, cancellation/refund persistence,) Tj
T*
(administrator permissions and safe database outage handling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Features not to be tested) Tj
T*
(Real gateway settlement, actual SMS/email delivery, bank-side refund settlement, hardware devices,) Tj
T*
(production failover and long-term uptime are not implemented or are out of scope. Do not record them) Tj
T*
(as passed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Test approach / strategy) Tj
T*
(- Unit: service validation, fare/refund calculations, error branches and rollback behavior using) Tj
T*
(isolated/mocked dependencies.) Tj
T*
(- Integration: run API and database operations on a dedicated disposable MySQL instance to verify) Tj
T*
(schema, constraints and transaction isolation.) Tj
T*
(- System: execute complete passenger and admin journeys via browser/API.) Tj
T*
(- Regression: run backend suite, frontend production build and browser suite on PRs.) Tj
T*
(- Performance: execute train-search benchmark with representative MySQL data and document P95) Tj
T*
(latency.) Tj
T*
(- Acceptance: demonstrate critical use cases and verify evidence against SRS IDs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Entry: stable build, configured test database, dummy accounts/trains/schedules and clean test data.) Tj
T*
(Exit: all planned critical cases executed; zero open critical defects; any unexecuted cases) Tj
T*
(explicitly marked; deviations approved. Do not infer test pass from source code alone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 Security validation) Tj
T*
(Verify password hashing and redaction; passenger ownership and admin RBAC; CSRF rejection; input) Tj
T*
(validation and SQL parameterization; production cookie/HTTPS configuration. Test) Tj
T*
(negative/unauthorized paths without using real customer data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Test environment) Tj
T*
(Python 3.10+, Node.js 20+, MySQL 8.0.16+, React/Vite and Django REST Framework. Tools: Python) Tj
T*
(unittest, compileall, npm build, Playwright, train-search benchmark, GitHub Actions. Test data:) Tj
T*
(dummy users \(passenger/admin\), stations, routes, schedules, fares, seats, bookings. Automated unit) Tj
T*
(tests use mocked database calls; separately run database integration tests for actual SQL) Tj
T*
(correctness.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Test schedule) Tj
T*
(Design and traceability: before freeze. Automated regression: each PR and final release candidate.) Tj
T*
(Integration and performance tests: final evaluation environment. Manual acceptance and video) Tj
T*
(capture: after stable release candidate. Actual dates and assignees are to be recorded by the team.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Test deliverables) Tj
T*
(This plan, test cases and scripts, test dataset, CI execution logs, defect log, unit/system) Tj
T*
(validation report, line and branch coverage reports, final test summary and sprint videos. See) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
