T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Roles and responsibilities) Tj
T*
(Developer: implement and unit-test assigned features. Reviewer/repository owner: review PRs and) Tj
T*
(approve merges. Test owner: execute acceptance and collect logs. Team: maintain traceability, defect) Tj
T*
(register, sprint videos and final sign-off. Individual names must be filled from the actual project) Tj
T*
(board.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Risks and mitigation) Tj
T*
(Mocked database tests can miss SQL integration failures: use disposable MySQL integration) Tj
T*
(environment. Browser automation may not prove accessibility: supplement manual checks. Concurrent) Tj
T*
(booking races are hard to reproduce: run deterministic lock/rollback tests. CI pass may be stale:) Tj
T*
(attach logs from the exact final commit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Assumptions and dependencies) Tj
T*
(MySQL schema and required migration scripts are installed; dummy data is available; production-like) Tj
T*
(environment is isolated from real users; external providers remain simulated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. Suspension and resumption) Tj
T*
(Suspend if test database unavailable, critical booking corruption occurs or a blocking build failure) Tj
T*
(prevents core scenarios. Resume after environment recovery, defect fix and successful smoke test.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
